Note for the implementer: annotations that name a SpEL/property placeholder (`topics = "${app.topic}"`) yield the literal `${app.topic}` — keep it, it is a stable join key across services that read the same property, and add nothing special. Multi-topic annotations (`topics = {"a","b"}`) are handled by Keyed returning the first literal; add a follow-up note rather than widening the rule here.

Marker: `eprintln!("[queues] annotation '{needle}' topic={topic} framework={framework:?} file={path}")`.

Tests: kafka_listener_topics_attr, rabbit_listener_queues_attr, sqs_listener_positional, nest_processor_queue_name, servicebus_trigger_attr, and a negative annotation_without_gate_is_ignored.

