**Lookup ladder**, `fn lookup_route(index, stripped, method, norm_path, prefixes) -> Vec<(RouteTarget, MatchTier)>`; return on the FIRST tier that yields anything (never union across tiers — that is where fan-out would come from):
1. `index[(method, path)]` → Exact.
2. `index[("ANY", path)]` → Any. (a). Also try `index[("ANY", stripped_path)]` inside tiers 3/4 rather than as a separate tier.
3. endpoint-side strip — today's loop, `index[(method|ANY, strip(path))]` → EndpointPrefix.
4. route-side strip — `stripped[(method|ANY, strip(path))]` → RoutePrefix. Covers client `/users` ↔ server `/api/users`.
5. base fold (c) — ONLY when `path` starts with the segment `{}` (i.e. the first segment came from an interpolation and is therefore a base URL, not a resource): `let folded = path.strip_prefix("/{}").unwrap_or(path)` (use `else { return vec![] }`, no unwrap on an Option that can be None) and re-run tiers 1-4 against `folded` → BaseFold.
6. suffix fallback (c) — ALSO gated on the leading-`{}` condition, so an ordinary path can never suffix-match. Walk suffixes of `folded` longest→shortest, require the suffix to retain at least one literal (non-`{}`) segment, take the FIRST tier-1..4 hit, and ABANDON if that key has more than 3 targets (ambiguous → emit nothing rather than fan out) → Suffix.

**Edge emission** at :1150-1158 becomes `confidence: weakest(weakest(n.confidence, target.confidence), tier.ceiling())`. Tiers 1-3 are today's semantics with an unchanged confidence, so no existing edge changes value.

**Marker**, last line of `resolve`:
`eprintln!("[http] routes={} endpoints={} paired={} (exact={} any={} eprefix={} rprefix={} base={} suffix={})", …)`.

