```rust
/// Request path for a CLIENT call literal, for parsers that reconstruct
/// interpolation themselves. Unlike `url_to_path` this never returns None —
/// it is a normaliser, not a filter, so no endpoint is ever lost:
///   `https://api.x/users?a=1` -> `/users`      (scheme+host+query dropped)
///   `/users?a=1#frag`          -> `/users`      (query+fragment dropped)
///   `${…}/users`               -> `${…}/users`  (interpolated base kept for the
///                                                resolver's BaseFold tier)
///   `auth/login`               -> `auth/login`  (relative hint, untouched)
///   `<unresolved>`             -> `<unresolved>`
/// Returns (path, changed) so the caller can record provenance.
pub fn normalise_client_path(raw: &str) -> (String, bool) { … }
```
Rules in order: return `(raw, false)` for `<unresolved>` or an empty string; if `raw` contains `"://"` take everything from the first `/` after the host (or `"/"` if none); then truncate at the first `?` or `#`; return `changed = result != raw`.

