**Dart.** At dart:569 replace the raw guard with
```rust
let (path, changed) = endpoint::normalise_client_path(&dart_string_path(sl, src));
if !path.starts_with('/') && !path.starts_with("${") { return; }
```
so an absolute URL now normalises into a real path and an interpolated-base path survives for A3.1's BaseFold tier, while a bare identifier or non-path first arg is still rejected. Add `raw: Option<String>` to `ClientEndpoint` (code-domain:711) and emit it from `endpoint_hit_json` (code-domain:737) under the same skip-if-none, which gives Go/Java/Python/Swift the field for free when they later adopt it.

