/// Best-effort source span for an HTTP node that carries no POSITION cell.
/// Reads an ENDPOINT_HIT cell (every language) or a JSON ROUTE_METHOD cell
/// (parser-go, ts_routes) and returns `(file, line0)` where `line0` is
/// ZERO-indexed to match POSITION's `start_line` (parsers/code/docs:29 stores
/// `start_position().row`, while these cells store `row + 1`). A `line` of 0
/// is ts_routes' 'unknown' placeholder and yields `None`.
pub fn http_node_span(cells: &[Cell]) -> Option<(String, Option<i64>)> { … }
```
Implementation: scan `cells` for `cell_type::ENDPOINT_HIT` first, then `cell_type::ROUTE_METHOD`; for each, if the payload is `Json(s) | Text(s)` parse with `serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>` (code-domain already depends on serde/serde_json) and take `file` (must be a non-empty string, else skip this cell) and `line`; map `line` via `n if n >= 1 => Some(n - 1)`, `_ => None`. Never unwrap; return None on any failure.

In `engine::locate_node`, after the existing POSITION loop (engine:1998) and inside the same `if let Some(n) = g.nodes.iter().find(...)` block:
```rust
if file.is_none() && matches!(kind_id, Some(k) if k == node_kind::ROUTE || k == node_kind::ENDPOINT) {
    if let Some((f, l)) = endpoint::http_node_span(&n.cells) {
        (file, line) = (Some(f), l);
        log_http_locate_once("cell", &qname);
    } else if kind_id == Some(node_kind::ROUTE) {
        // Tier 3: thirteen parsers write ROUTE_METHOD as bare Text with no
        // file (clojure/csharp/dart/elixir/php/java/ruby/rust/scala/swift/
        // python). Borrow the span of the handler the route is HANDLED_BY —
        // 'where is this route defined' is answered by its handler. Scan is
        // confined to this repo's own edge list; HANDLED_BY never crosses repos.
        for e in &g.edges {
            if e.from != id || e.category != edge_category::HANDLED_BY { continue; }
            if let Some(h) = g.nodes.iter().find(|h| h.id == e.to)
                && let Some(p) = position_of(h) { (file, line) = (Some(p.0), Some(p.1)); log_http_locate_once("handled_by", &qname); break; }
        }
    }
}
```
Factor the existing POSITION parse at :1986-1997 into a small `fn position_of(n: &Node) -> Option<(String, i64)>` so tier 3 reuses it rather than duplicating the JSON scan; that is a pure refactor of code already in the function.

**Marker**, once per process so the hot loops do not flood:
```rust
static HTTP_LOCATE_LOGGED: std::sync::Once = std::sync::Once::new();
fn log_http_locate_once(source: &str, qname: &str) {
    HTTP_LOCATE_LOGGED.call_once(|| eprintln!("[locate] http span fallback fired: source={source} node={qname}"));
}
```

Explicit NON-goal, to keep the blast radius small: `projection_text::node_position` (projection-text/src/lib.rs:552) and therefore the pyo3 `nodes_json` `path`/`start_line` fields are NOT changed here. Changing them would alter dense-text bytes for every repo with HTTP nodes and put pressure on the determinism gate (engine/tests/byte_identical.rs). Record it as the follow-up so the next session does not assume it landed.

