```rust
/// FastAPI dependency injection. Two spellings, both blind today because the
/// call lives in a parameter DEFAULT or inside an `Annotated[...]` subscript,
/// and `collect_calls_in` only walks the function body:
///
///   def read(db: Session = Depends(get_db)):            # typed_default_parameter.value
///   def read(db = Depends(get_db)):                      # default_parameter.value
///   def read(db: Annotated[Session, Depends(get_db)]):   # type -> subscript
///
/// The INJECTS target is the *provider* (`get_db`), not the annotation type —
/// that is what FastAPI actually wires and what `trace` needs to walk. The
/// annotation type keeps its existing USES ref from `collect_type_refs`.
fn collect_depends_refs(def: TsNode, src: &[u8], from: NodeId, module_id: NodeId, acc: &mut Acc) {
    let Some(params) = def.child_by_field_name("parameters") else { return; };
    let mut seen: std::collections::HashSet<String> = Default::default();
    let mut cursor = params.walk();
    for p in params.named_children(&mut cursor) {
        match p.kind() {
            "default_parameter" | "typed_default_parameter" => {
                if let Some(v) = p.child_by_field_name("value") {
                    push_depends_target(v, src, from, module_id, &mut seen, acc);
                }
            }
            _ => {}
        }
        // `Annotated[T, Depends(f)]` — the marker lives inside the type.
        if let Some(ty) = p.child_by_field_name("type") {
            scan_annotated_depends(ty, src, from, module_id, &mut seen, acc);
        }
    }
}
```

`fn push_depends_target(expr, src, from, module_id, seen, acc)`: require `expr.kind() == "call"`; read `expr.child_by_field_name("function")` and accept it when its text's trailing dotted segment is one of `["Depends", "Security", "Provide"]` (`Depends`/`Security` are FastAPI, `Provide` is dependency-injector — all three are the same shape, and matching on the trailing segment covers `fastapi.Depends`). Then take the first named child of `expr.child_by_field_name("arguments")`; accept `identifier` (take its text) or `attribute` (take the `attribute` field's text, matching the existing convention at :1272-1274). Skip when `is_type_noise(name)` or `!seen.insert(name.to_string())`. Push `UnresolvedRef { from, from_module: module_id, qualifier: CallQualifier::Bare(name), category: edge_category::INJECTS }` and `di_stats::record(DiShape::PyFastapiDepends)`.

Bare `Depends()` with no argument (FastAPI infers from the annotation) falls back to the annotation type: when `arguments` has no named child, use the sibling `type` field's first identifier via the existing `emit_type_idents` traversal shape. Keep this branch simple — if nothing is derivable, emit nothing.

`fn scan_annotated_depends(ty, src, from, module_id, seen, acc)`: a small explicit stack walk over `ty` (same pattern as `emit_type_idents` at :1256-1304) that, on encountering a node of kind `"call"`, hands it to `push_depends_target` and does NOT descend further into it. Everything else pushes its named children. This handles `Annotated[Session, Depends(get_db)]` and nested `Optional[Annotated[...]]`.

Wire it in `visit_function` at :570, right after `collect_return_type_ref`:

```rust
    // FastAPI `Depends(...)` in parameter defaults / Annotated markers.
    collect_depends_refs(n, src, func_id, module_id, acc);
```

