In graph/src/lib.rs, first generalise the JSON field reader: `fn extract_str_field<'a>(json: &'a str, key: &str) -> Option<&'a str>` — same tight scan as today's extract_method_field (find `"<key>"`, then `:`, then the quoted value), and `fn extract_method_field(json: &str) -> Option<&str> { extract_str_field(json, "method") }`. This keeps the graph crate off serde_json exactly as the comment at graph:1255-1258 demands.

Then:
```rust
/// Pair contract operations (OpenAPI/Swagger DOC_SECTIONs carrying ORIGIN
/// provenance=contract) to the ROUTE nodes that implement them. Strong on an
/// exact (method, path) hit; Medium when the match needed the api/v1 prefix
/// stripped or the server base dropped.
pub fn link_contract_routes(merged: &mut MergedGraph) {
    let index = build_route_index(&merged.graphs);
    if index.is_empty() { return; }
    let (mut ops, mut exact, mut prefix) = (0usize, 0usize, 0usize);
    let mut new_edges: Vec<Edge> = Vec::new();
    for g in &merged.graphs {
        for n in &g.nodes {
            if g.nav.kind_by_id.get(&n.id) != Some(&node_kind::DOC_SECTION) { continue }
            let Some(origin) = n.cells.iter().find(|c| c.kind == cell_type::ORIGIN) else { continue };
            let CellPayload::Json(j) = &origin.payload else { continue };
            if extract_str_field(j, "provenance") != Some("contract") { continue }
            let Some(method) = extract_str_field(j, "method") else { continue };
            let Some(path) = extract_str_field(j, "path") else { continue };
            ops += 1;
            let method = method.to_ascii_uppercase();
            let norm = normalise_http_path(path);
            // 1. exact
            let (targets, conf): (&[RouteTarget], Confidence) = match index.get(&(method.clone(), norm.clone())) {
                Some(t) => { exact += 1; (t.as_slice(), Confidence::Strong) }
                None => {
                    // 2. api/v1 prefix strip (covers an OpenAPI `servers: /api/v1` base)
                    let mut t = lookup_route_with_prefix_strip(&index, &method, &norm);
                    // 3. the raw, pre-join path (covers a non-API-shaped server base)
                    if t.is_empty() && let Some(raw) = extract_str_field(j, "raw_path") {
                        let raw_norm = normalise_http_path(raw);
                        if raw_norm != norm { t = index.get(&(method.clone(), raw_norm)).map(|v| v.as_slice()).unwrap_or(&[]); }
                    }
                    if t.is_empty() { continue }
                    prefix += 1;
                    (t, Confidence::Medium)
                }
            };
            for t in targets {
                new_edges.push(Edge { from: n.id, to: t.route_id, category: edge_category::DOCUMENTS, confidence: weakest(conf, t.confidence) });
            }
        }
    }
    if ops > 0 { eprintln!("[contract-link] ops={ops} exact={exact} prefix={prefix}"); }
    merged.cross_edges.extend(new_edges);
}
```
Direction is contract→ROUTE so `governing_docs(route_qname)` (engine:1939-1964, which collects `e.to == target && category == DOCUMENTS`) returns the contract op with no change to that primitive. Iteration is over `merged.graphs` / `g.nodes` (Vecs) so emission order is deterministic; post_passes sorts cross_edges afterwards regardless (engine:521-523).

